  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project to Develop A Sustainable Agricultural Environment Through the Organization of Durian Producers Cooperative In Mindanao, Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 Implementation of production technology training, 1.2 Climate change data collection, 2.1 Recruitment of Organization members, 2.2 Establishment of Organization manual, 2.3 Implementation of a Organization capacity building program, 3.1 Development of Durian Sales Strategy Based on Market Research Data, 3.2 Establishment of production organization collection/processing/distribution infrastructure, 3.3 Production of infrastructure operation manuals including management methods</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development strategies in the Philippines and business areas are consistent with Korea&apos;s ODA support plan. Mindanao accounts for 35% of Philippine agricultural production but has the highest poverty rate of 36%. Establishment of international, national, and regional development strategies and support plans to solve problems. Mindanao Development Agency, local governments, and resident organizations all emphasize the need for projects in planned areas and express their willingness to cooperate.1.&#xb450;&#xb9ac;&#xc548; &#xc0dd;&#xc0b0;&#xc790; &#xc870;&#xc9c1; &#xad6c;&#xc131;,  2.&#xb450;&#xb9ac;&#xc548; &#xd310;&#xb9e4;&#xc2dc;&#xc7a5; &#xac1c;&#xbc1c;</narrative>
  </description>
